[Chapter "Two Knights Attack"]
[Line "Quiet 6.d3"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defense: Two Knights Attack, Mindeno Variation, Exchange Line"]

{White keeps the centre closed and plays slowly. Black develops naturally.} 1. e4 c6 {The Caro-Kann.} 2. Nc3 d5 {Challenge e4.} 3. Nf3 Bg4 {Pin the knight.} 4. h3 Bxf3 {Give the bishop for the knight.} 5. Qxf3 e6 {Solid centre.} 6. d3 Nd7 {Flexible: the other knight can go to f6 or e7, and ...e5 stays possible.} 7. Be2 Ngf6 {Develop.} 8. O-O Be7 {Safe development; Black castles next with an easy game.} *
